name issue_895_red_sender_report_sync
describe issue_12_lossbwe_shallow's link: the audio SR's RTP time as libwebrtc stamps it with RED, so A/V sync delays audio as libwebrtc's does (#895)
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=20ms
# Issue #895: with RED (the default), libwebrtc's audio sender report extrapolates the RTP timestamp at
# kBogusRtpRateForAudioRtcp, 8 kHz, in whole ms (RTCPSender::BuildSR; RED's payload type has no registered rate).
# Ours used 48 kHz in microseconds, so the receiver's RTP-to-NTP mapping for audio, the relative delay and
# RtpStreamsSynchronizer's filtered diff came out 5-9 ms lower than libwebrtc's, its +15 ms audio delay steps
# (28 s and 34 s on seed 1) never happened, and the audio cells sat ahead of libwebrtc's.
# Seed 1: main 70 ms / 125.0 ms, fixed 100 / 155.0, libwebrtc 100 / 155.2. Seeds 1-10, jb_delay_p95: main
# 70 80 80 80 70 80 80 70 90 90 (mean 79), fixed 100 100 100 90 90 90 90 90 90 100 (94), libwebrtc 100 100 80
# 100 100 90 100 90 110 90 (96); mouth_to_ear_p95: main mean 134.1, fixed 149.1, libwebrtc 151.0.
expect audio.jb_delay_p95_ms >= 90
expect audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms >= 144
expect audio.interruptions <= 3
